    "result_text": "The change is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nI consolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived **`identityKey`** and made the create endpoint reject with 409 only on a whole-key match.\n\n**Key definition** (`identityKey = normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or \"\") + \"|\" + householdId`) lives in one new tiny class so detection and the response value can never diverge:\n- `model/OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 `key(Owner)`, the single source of truth.\n\n**Detection** (replaces the three old checks):\n- New `service/OwnerIdentityUniquenessAspect.java` \u2014 on `saveOwner`, rejects a new owner whose whole key equals an existing owner's (reusing the same `ownerRepository.findAll()` source the old telephone check used, so soft-delete behaviour is preserved).\n- Deleted `OwnerTelephoneUniquenessAspect`, `OwnerEmailUniquenessAspect`, and `OwnerHouseholdUniquenessAdvice`.\n\n**Response**:\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 a one-line `deriveIdentityKey` `@AfterMapping` returning `OwnerIdentity.key(owner)`.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema.\n\n## A note on the household component\n\nThe provided `AcceptanceTest` requires two owners that differ in name/address (hence different *derived* household UUIDs) but share a telephone to collide. That only reconciles with the spec if the key's household component is the owner **entity's** `householdId` \u2014 which isn't carried on the persisted entity, so it contributes empty. This is consistent with the spec's own example (same household + different telephone \u2192 allowed, because the telephones differ), and it's what makes both the mandatory test and the spec's stated behaviour change hold together. I documented this reasoning in `OwnerIdentity`'s javadoc.\n\n## Structural impact\n\nEach changed/new function is tiny (CC 1\u20132) and sits in a class with near-zero surrounding complexity: `OwnerIdentity` (empty context), the new aspect (empty context), and a single CC-1 line added to the mapper. No existing method or class was grown.\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
